---
---

<section class="industry">
  <div class="container industry__split">
    <div class="industry__media" data-reveal data-parallax-wrap data-industry-media>
      <img
        class="industry__media-img industry__media-img--1"
        src="/images/industry-professionals-bg.jpg"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
        data-parallax-image
      />
      <img
        class="industry__media-img industry__media-img--2"
        src="/images/industry-professionals-bg-2.jpg"
        alt=""
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="industry__text">
      <div class="industry__block" data-reveal>
        <h2 class="industry__heading" data-reveal-heading>Industry Expertise</h2>
        <p class="industry__body">
          We understand the challenges faced by network operators and the expertise required to
          drive operational success. That's why CHIME was developed with insights from professionals
          across the industry, ensuring it meets the real-world needs of those working on the front
          lines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="industry__block" data-reveal data-industry-frame-2>
        <h2 class="industry__heading" data-reveal-heading>Industry Professionals</h2>
        <p class="industry__body">
          At the heart of every successful network operation are the dedicated professionals who
          bring expertise, precision, and innovation to their roles. From design and construction to
          maintenance and oversight, these specialists ensure the seamless function and evolution of
          critical infrastructure.
        </p>
        <p class="industry__body">
          CHIME is built on the collective experience of these industry experts, offering solutions
          to those shaping the future of network operations.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .industry {
    background: var(--color-white);
  }

  /* Narrower than the page's own container (global.css) — this section
     reads as a contained two-column block, not a full-width band. */
  .industry__split {
    max-width: 68rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 4rem;
    padding-block: 7rem;
  }

  /* Sticky while the (now taller, two-block) text column scrolls past it -
     align-items: flex-start above keeps this column at its own natural
     height instead of stretching to match the text column, which is what
     gives the sticky effect room to work. */
  .industry__media {
    position: sticky;
    top: 6rem;
    flex: 0 0 28.75rem;
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    border-radius: 24px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: linear-gradient(160deg, var(--color-grey-100), #dce9f2 55%, #c9e4f0);
  }

  /* Sized 116% with a matching negative inset so the scroll-parallax drift
     (--parallax-y, from image-parallax.ts) and the hover-zoom (--hover-scale)
     never uncover the frame's edges. Both live on custom properties, not
     the transform property itself, so the two effects compose instead of
     one overwriting the other's inline style. */
  .industry__media-img {
    position: absolute;
    inset: -8%;
    width: 116%;
    height: 116%;
    object-fit: cover;
    transition: opacity 0.6s ease;
  }

  .industry__media-img--1 {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(var(--parallax-y, 0px)) scale(var(--hover-scale, 1));
  }

  .industry__media-img--2 {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  /* Toggled by industry-crossfade.ts once the second text block scrolls
     into view. */
  .industry__media.is-frame-2 .industry__media-img--1 {
    opacity: 0;
  }

  .industry__media.is-frame-2 .industry__media-img--2 {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .industry__media:hover img {
    --hover-scale: 1.04;
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .industry__media-img {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  .industry__text {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24rem;
  }

  /* Both blocks get a min-height matching the sticky image beside them
     (28.75rem wide × 4:5 aspect-ratio = 35.9375rem tall) with their text
     centred inside it. For the second block this also means the text
     column stays tall enough that the image's sticky lock doesn't
     release until this text is centred in the viewport too, rather than
     the image scrolling away right as the second block appears. */
  .industry__block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    min-height: 35.9375rem;
  }

  .industry__heading {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  .industry__body {
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-grey-600);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .industry__split {
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    .industry__media {
      position: static;
    }

    .industry__block {
      min-height: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
